    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0425" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6474/12–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-17T17:00:00-05:00">December 17,
                            1945—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>405. Dept continues to adhere to view expressed Deptel 20, Jan 25 that it is
                    unnecessary and undesirable for enemy states to have direct diplomatic relations
                    between themselves so long as they remain under armistice regimes. Brit and
                    Soviet Govt expressed agreement this attitude at that time.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, message contained urtel 750, Dec 11<anchor n="48" xml:id="d423-f1"/>
                    should not be transmitted to Hungarian Govt.</p>
                <p>Sent to Sofia, rptd to Budapest.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d423-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d423-f1" n="48" xml:id="d423-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported a message regarding proposed renewal of diplomatic
                    relations between Bulgaria and Hungary which a representative of the Hungarian
                    colony in Sofia wished to have communicated to the Hungarian Government
                    (701.6474/12–1145).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d423-f2" n="49" xml:id="d423-f2-content">
                <p>As No. 835.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
